 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Review `review-8e48265b8c9215ac` — bounded learnability finding
+
+Production `generator.py` was left unchanged (SHA-256
+`05fdaf7316a8252378f484b9b5e38b69fb1fca2b4263cf50de4e9eb770474c32`).
+A task-local independent probe was added at `workspace/learnability_probe.py`
+with two portable regression tests.
+
+The executable rival swaps only the legend meanings of token 2 (rotate-CW) and
+token 4 (transpose). It fits 0/5 labeled canonical pairs, but agreed with the
+canonical rule on 563/1000 ordinary generated inputs: easy 198/334, medium
+195/333, hard 170/333. This creates an episode-level teaching hole even though
+the canonical examples themselves are sufficient.
+
+A retained two-demonstration witness uses ordinary draws 1 and 5; both the
+canonical and rival Racket programs produce the same labels. Draw 7 is a query
+where the programs differ by 12 cells. The packet's protected Racket backend
+executed both programs on all three inputs (6 evaluations), and the independent
+Python transcription matched those labels. Evidence is retained in
+`counterexamples/review-8e48265b8c9215ac/learnability.json` and
+`checks/12ec29eae990/learnability.json`.
+
+Concrete next repair: in episode assembly, require at least one demonstration
+with an asymmetric motif and an interior anchor using token 2 or 4 for which
+rotate-CW and transpose give different unclipped stamps. This can be done by
+constructive selection without changing the rule or increasing the demo count.
+The finite rival finding is not a universal ambiguity proof, owner acceptance,
+or training admission.
